  "author": "Apple Inc.",
  "note": "Apple's default macOS and iOS wallpapers as light/dark pairs, and the Mac OS X Nature desktop pictures as single photographs. Apple retains rights to this artwork; it is committed here for a personal site, not licensed onward. The archives the files were pulled from (ryOS included, which is AGPL-3.0) do not license Apple's images either, and their repository licenses are not asserted to do so. Resolution rule: every committed full-size file must cover a 2560x1600 viewport with at most a 1.07x stretch, and is downscaled to the smallest size that still covers it, never upscaled. Photographs also ship 1280x800 and 1920x1200 cover renditions — Nature stills and the Catalina / Mojave pairs. iOS 27 (1320x2868), iOS 18 (1480x3192 / 1661x3600), iOS 17 (2048x2048) and portrait iPadOS 26/27 (2064x2752) fell short and were left out; iPadOS 26 is the landscape home-screen still. Derivatives: graphic release pairs are WebP q80; photographs WebP q95 with 4:4:4 chroma (q90 if a file would exceed 1.8MB — the q75 encode crushed smooth skies); thumbnails at most 480px at q72. HEIC frames are zero-indexed. Nothing is cropped: every committed file keeps its source aspect. The Nature photographs carry Photoshop timestamps from August 2007, the Mac OS X Leopard cycle; the individual releases they shipped with are not verified. Clown Fish and Ladybug were dropped from the catalog. High-resolution originals were collected from: wallpapers.poutanen.dev (macOS 6K graphic pairs), 4kwallpapers.com (Golden Gate native 4480x3088, Catalina 6016x6016, Mojave 5120x2880, iOS 15 2916x2916, iPadOS 18 3840x2668), static.applewalls.com (iPadOS 26 landscape), LAYTAT/macOS-Wallpapers and benediktkr/Deeeee-macOS-Wallpapers (untouched /System/Desktop Pictures dumps), 512pixels.net (classic defaults; 6K files there are hand-upscales and are not used), iClarified and wallpapers.ispazio.net (beta stills). Portrait iPhone lock-screens never cover 2560x1600.",
